# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Energy IoT Platform — repository ignore rules
#
#  This tree is a LIVE PRODUCTION DIRECTORY. The backend, the monitoring
#  scheduler and both static servers run from these paths. The rules below
#  exist first to keep operational state and secrets out of version control,
#  and only second to keep the repository tidy.
#
#  Before relaxing any rule in the "Secrets" or "Operational state" sections,
#  read docs/Security.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real credentials live in .env; the committed template is .env.example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/public.key
secrets.json
smart-plugs.conf
!smart-plugs.conf.template

# ── Operational state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The platform database is ~180 MB of live measurements in WAL mode. It is
# never committed; it is reproduced with `python -m migrations.runner`.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
monitoring_watchdog.json
# Operator-editable runtime config: the live copy is mutated through the
# Settings UI, so only the committed template tracks its shape.
runtime_platform_settings.json
!runtime_platform_settings.example.json
monitoring_config.json
!monitoring_config.example.json

# ── Backups ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Point-in-time copies taken by the operator. Several GB; never in git.
backups/
**/backups/
*_backup_*/
app_backup_*/
src_backup_*/
*.bak
*.bak_*
*-before-*
pre-standardize-*/

# ── Build output and dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

venv/
.venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ── Generated artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
generated_reports/
edge/reports/
docs/deployments/
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Machine-learning models ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Retrained from data; large, binary, and not meaningfully diffable.
*.joblib
*.pkl
models/*.h5

# ── OS and editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `._*` are macOS AppleDouble forks left by an SMB copy; they carry no content.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── On-box staging checkout ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `frontend-src/` is a second checkout of the frontend, byte-identical to
# `frontend/src`, served on :5175 as the review environment before a change is
# repeated in production. It is a deployment artefact of this particular host,
# not a second codebase, so only `frontend/` is tracked.
# See docs/Deployment.md § Staging.
frontend-src/

# ── Scratch files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
part[0-9].txt
test.txt
patch_frontend_safe.py
patch_backend_real_data.py
clean_seed_data.py

# Node software: the rendered per-node network config holds the AP passphrase.
# Only the redacted .example is tracked; real renders never enter the repo.
edge/node/net/config/network.yaml
